# C.S. Lewis touches for each night.
#   pic  = "Picture this": a short lead-in to the story, told the way Lewis explains things
#          (a picture or a "suppose" first, then the point). Narnia scenes are retold in our own words.
#   line = optional "Lewis line": (quote, source, how it ties to tonight).
# Only real, verified Lewis quotes, kept short. Everything is read through a Lutheran (LCMS) lens:
# we use the parts of Lewis that agree with Scripture and the Catechism.
MC="Mere Christianity"; LWW="The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe"; PC="Prince Caspian"; VDT="The Voyage of the Dawn Treader"
SC="The Silver Chair"; HHB="The Horse and His Boy"; MN="The Magician’s Nephew"; LB="The Last Battle"; WG="The Weight of Glory"
LEWIS={
"2026-11-16":("Suppose someone built a wall to keep a river from ever reaching the sea. The water would just find another way: under, around, through a crack nobody noticed. God’s plans are like that river. Tonight a king tries to stop God, and God slips right past him with a little basket.",None),
"2026-11-17":("In Narnia, when the children first hear that Aslan is a lion, Susan asks if he’s safe. Mr. Beaver laughs at the question. A lion is not something you tame, he says, but Aslan is good. Moses is about to meet Someone like that: so holy he has to take off his shoes, and so good He comes to rescue His people.",
  ("’Course he isn’t safe. But he’s good. He’s the King, I tell you.",LWW,"God is holy, not tame. And He is good, which is why Moses didn’t have to be afraid to listen.")),
"2026-11-18":("In The Magician’s Nephew, Aslan sings Narnia into being. The children hear the most beautiful song in the world. But grumpy Uncle Andrew, who doesn’t want Aslan to be real, hears only roaring and growling. He tells himself it’s just noise until he can’t hear the song at all. Pharaoh did the same thing with God’s Word.",None),
"2026-11-19":("In Narnia, Edmund betrays his brother and sisters, and the White Witch says the law gives her his life. Then Aslan quietly takes Edmund’s place. He walks to the Stone Table by himself and dies there instead of the traitor. The next morning the Table cracks and Aslan is alive. Tonight’s story is the first picture of that: a lamb dies, and death passes over.",
  ("Death itself would start working backwards.",LWW,"Aslan’s death for Edmund is a picture of Jesus, our Passover Lamb, who died in our place and rose again.")),
"2026-11-20":("Picture being stuck at the bottom of a deep well. Trying harder, jumping higher, or being smarter won’t get you out. Somebody has to lower a rope and pull. Israel is stuck between an army and an ocean tonight, and all they can do is watch God pull them through.",None),
"2026-11-21":("Imagine a car that was built to run on gas, and someone tries to fill it with orange juice. It won’t go, no matter how good the juice is. Lewis said people are like that: God made us to run on Him. Tonight God feeds His people bread from heaven, and Jesus says He Himself is that Bread.",
  ("God cannot give us a happiness and peace apart from Himself, because it is not there.",MC,"Lewis used the car picture himself. We were made to be filled by God, and in Jesus, the Bread of Life, He fills us.")),
"2026-11-22":("In The Silver Chair, Aslan gives Jill four signs to help her on a hard journey, and tells her to say them every morning and every night so she won’t forget. Later, when she’s cold and tired, she stops saying them and starts missing them. God gave Israel His commandments the same way: after He rescued them, as a gift for the road.",
  ("Remember, remember, remember the Signs.",SC,"That’s why we say the Catechism every night: so God’s Word is in us when we need it.")),
"2026-11-23":("Suppose a general told his army to win a battle by taking a walk and blowing some trumpets. Everyone would laugh. But God often does the most important things in the plainest ways: water, bread, a few words. Tonight God knocks down a city with a parade.",None),
"2026-11-24":("Picture a little kid “helping” his dad carry a couch. The dad lifts the whole thing, and the kid holds one corner and grins. When it’s done, everyone knows who did the heavy lifting. Gideon’s army is about to get very small, so everyone will know who won.",
  ("As long as you are looking down, you cannot see something that is above you.",MC,"Lewis was talking about pride. God made Gideon small so Israel would look up.")),
"2026-11-25":("Lewis noticed that people love to praise what they enjoy: a great catch, a beautiful sunset, a really good pizza. Saying it out loud isn’t extra. It’s part of the enjoying. Tonight ten men are healed, but only one comes back to say so.",
  ("Praise not merely expresses but completes the enjoyment.","Reflections on the Psalms","Thanking God isn’t a chore. It finishes the joy of His gifts.")),
"2026-11-26":("Imagine a kid on Christmas morning who opens every present and never once looks at who gave them. He has the gifts but misses the giver. Thanksgiving turns our eyes from the gifts to the One who gives them, even after a hard year.",
  ("We are far too easily pleased.",WG,"Lewis meant we settle for small things when God wants to give us Himself. That’s the biggest reason for thanks.")),
"2026-11-27":("When a little kid scrapes a knee, he doesn’t make a polite speech. He runs to Mom or Dad crying, and that’s exactly right. Hannah prays tonight like that child: no fancy words, just her whole heart.",None),
"2026-11-28":("Suppose you had a letter from someone who loved you very much, and you left it on the counter unopened for a year. Lewis would say the letter didn’t stop talking; you stopped listening. Samuel is about to learn to say, “Speak, Lord.”",None),
"2026-11-29":("In Narnia, the White Witch made it always winter and never Christmas. For a hundred years everyone waited. Then one day the snow started dripping and the whisper went around: Aslan is on the move. Advent begins today, and tonight the King rides into Jerusalem.",
  ("Aslan is on the move.",LWW,"Advent is the season of “the King is coming.” Jesus came, comes to us in His Word and Supper, and will come again.")),
"2026-11-30":("Lewis said there are no ordinary people. Every person you meet is someone who will live forever. So the kid nobody picks, the little brother, the quiet one at the end of the row, is never just ordinary to God. Tonight Samuel learns that God sees the heart.",
  ("There are no ordinary people. You have never talked to a mere mortal.",WG,"God chose David when everyone overlooked him. Nobody is overlooked by God.")),
"2026-12-01":("In Narnia, Peter is still just a boy when a huge wolf attacks his sister. He’s scared and his sword feels heavy, but he runs at the wolf anyway, and Aslan stands behind him. David walks toward a giant tonight with only a sling, and the Lord of hosts is behind him.",None),
"2026-12-02":("Picture a shepherd standing between his sheep and a lion. Lewis would ask: what kind of shepherd is that? Not one who only feeds the sheep, but one who would get hurt to keep them safe. That’s the Shepherd David sings about tonight.",None),
"2026-12-03":("Lewis said the greatest wonder of Christmas is that the God who made the whole universe didn’t just become a man; He became a baby first. Suppose the author of a book wrote himself into the story as a newborn. That’s what Isaiah promises tonight.",
  ("The Son of God became a man to enable men to become sons of God.",MC,"Jesus became like us so that in Baptism we could be made God’s children.")),
"2026-12-04":("In Narnia, the great kings and queens weren’t giants or warriors. They were four ordinary kids from England. God loves to use small things. Tonight we hear about a tiny town too small to matter, where the King would be born.",None),
"2026-12-05":("Imagine running away from a friend who wants to help you, ducking into an alley, only to find that friend already waiting at the other end. Jonah tries to run from God tonight, and finds out God is everywhere, even inside a fish.",
  ("God whispers to us in our pleasures, speaks in our conscience, but shouts in our pains.","The Problem of Pain","God used Jonah’s trouble to call him back, and He can use our hard times the same way.")),
"2026-12-06":("Lewis once said the only safe rule for giving is to give more than you can spare. He didn’t mean giving to show off. He meant giving the way God gives: freely, more than enough, without keeping score. Bishop Nicholas gave like that, in secret.",
  ("I am afraid the only safe rule is to give more than we can spare.",MC,"Nicholas gave freely because Jesus had given him everything.")),
"2026-12-07":("Suppose two teams said, “Whoever’s god is real, let him light the fire.” One team shouts and dances all day and nothing happens. The other soaks the wood with water and prays one simple prayer. Lewis would say the real God doesn’t need the noise. Tonight fire falls on Mount Carmel.",None),
"2026-12-08":("In Narnia, things never happen the same way twice, Aslan tells Lucy. He doesn’t always come when or how we expect. Zechariah had prayed for years and figured the answer was no. Tonight an angel shows up with a yes.",
  ("Things never happen the same way twice.",PC,"God hears every prayer, and He answers in His own time and His own way.")),
"2026-12-09":("Lewis said faith is holding on to what you’ve been told is true, even when your feelings waver. Mary didn’t understand how God would do it. But God had said it, and that was enough for her. Tonight an angel visits a young girl in Nazareth.",None),
"2026-12-10":("Lewis pointed out that the God who made everything became not just a baby, but before that, a tiny unborn child. Think how small that is! Tonight an unborn baby jumps for joy, because an even tinier unborn Baby has come near.",
  ("The Eternal Being, who knows everything and who created the whole universe, became not only a man but (before that) a baby.",MC,"Jesus was once smaller than any of us. Every baby, born and unborn, is precious to Him.")),
"2026-12-11":("Picture a signpost on a trail. Nobody hikes to admire the signpost. Its whole job is to point to where you’re going. Lewis would say John’s life was a signpost, and tonight his dad sings about where it points.",None),
"2026-12-12":("Real goodness often looks quiet: no speeches, no applause, just doing the right thing when nobody’s watching. Joseph is about to have a very hard choice, and he listens to God.",None),
"2026-12-13":("At the very end of the world in The Voyage of the Dawn Treader, the children find a Lamb cooking breakfast for them by the water. As they watch, the Lamb turns into Aslan, who tells them that in our world they must learn to know Him by another name. Tonight John points and says who that is: the Lamb of God.",
  ("…that by knowing me here for a little, you may know me better there.",VDT,"Lewis wrote Aslan to help us know Jesus better. The real Lamb of God takes away the sin of the world.")),
"2026-12-14":("In Narnia, after a hundred years of winter, the children hear a strange sound: dripping. Then the trickle of streams, then birds, then flowers pushing up through the snow. Spring came where everything looked dead. Tonight Isaiah promises a green shoot from a dead stump.",
  ("Wrong will be right, when Aslan comes in sight.",LWW,"When Jesus comes, dead things come alive again.")),
"2026-12-15":("In Prince Caspian, Aslan tells Caspian that being a child of Adam and Eve is honor enough to lift the head of the poorest beggar, and shame enough to bow the head of the greatest king. Jesus’ family tree has kings and heroes, and also some big sinners. Tonight we see why.",
  ("You come of the Lord Adam and the Lady Eve.",PC,"Jesus isn’t ashamed to call sinners His family. That includes us.")),
"2026-12-16":("Picture a little lamb that gets tired on a long walk. A good shepherd doesn’t yell at it. He picks it up and carries it close. Lewis would say: look at what God is like before you decide what you think of Him. Tonight Isaiah shows us.",None),
"2026-12-17":("Suppose a king wanted to help his poorest village. He could send money or a messenger. Or he could take off his crown, move into the village, and live there himself. Lewis loved that Christmas is the third one. Tonight’s name says it all: Immanuel.",
  ("He is building a palace. He intends to come and live in it Himself.",MC,"God didn’t just send help. He came to live with us, and in us.")),
"2026-12-18":("Lewis said he believed in Jesus the way he believed the sun had risen: not only because he could see it, but because by its light he could see everything else. Tonight Isaiah promises a great light for people sitting in the dark.",
  ("I believe in Christianity as I believe that the sun has risen: not only because I see it, but because by it I see everything else.","“Is Theology Poetry?”","Jesus is the Light that helps us see everything else rightly.")),
"2026-12-19":("In The Horse and His Boy, Shasta has a long, scary trip full of things going wrong. Only at the end does he learn the lion that kept showing up, pushing him along and keeping him safe, was Aslan the whole time. Mary and Joseph are on a hard road tonight, and God is guiding every step.",
  ("I tell no one any story but his own.",HHB,"God is writing your story too, and He is with you on every road.")),
"2026-12-20":("Picture the last day of a long road trip. Somebody spots the first sign with your town’s name on it, and the whole car cheers. Lewis would say Christian joy is like that: the trip isn’t over, but home is close. Tonight: The Lord is at hand!",None),
"2026-12-21":("Lewis said people sometimes call Jesus a good teacher, but that’s the one thing He didn’t leave room for. Anyone who said what Jesus said is either lying, or confused, or He is exactly who He says. Thomas finally sees the risen Jesus tonight and makes his choice.",
  ("Either this man was, and is, the Son of God: or else a madman or something worse.",MC,"Thomas chose: “My Lord and my God!” That baby in the manger is God.")),
"2026-12-22":("Imagine a long, dark night when you can’t sleep. Then a thin line of gold shows up at the edge of the sky, and you know the night won’t last. Zechariah calls Jesus “the sunrise from on high.”",None),
"2026-12-23":("Good storytellers set everything up long before the big moment of a story. God is the greatest Author. He promised a Savior in the garden and kept setting things up for thousands of years, until the exact right time.",None),
"2026-12-24":("Near the end of Narnia, Lucy steps into an old stable and finds that the inside is bigger than the outside. She says that in our world, too, a stable once held something bigger than the whole world. Tonight is that night.",
  ("In our world too, a Stable once had something inside it that was bigger than our whole world.",LB,"The God who holds the whole world was held in Mary’s arms.")),
"2026-12-25":("In Narnia, Christmas finally comes because Aslan is coming back. Father Christmas shows up with gifts, and the long winter starts to melt. Here, Christmas is the day the King Himself arrives, and the best gift is Him.",
  ("Always winter and never Christmas.",LWW,"That was Narnia without Aslan. Because Jesus is born, it’s never “never Christmas” for us.")),
"2026-12-26":("Lewis said everyone thinks forgiveness is a lovely idea until they have something to forgive. Stephen had something enormous to forgive tonight, and he did it, because Jesus had forgiven him first.",
  ("Every one says forgiveness is a lovely idea, until they have something to forgive.",MC,"Real forgiveness is hard, and Jesus gives us strength to do it.")),
"2026-12-27":("Lewis said Christians don’t think God loves us because we’re good, but that God will make us good because He loves us. John learned that. He was once called a “Son of Thunder,” and Jesus’ love turned him into the apostle of love.",
  ("God will make us good because He loves us.",MC,"God’s love comes first. It isn’t a prize for being good; it’s what makes us new.")),
"2026-12-28":("Lewis called this world “enemy-occupied territory,” and said Christianity is the story of the rightful King landing in disguise to win it back. Even at Christmas there was an enemy: King Herod. But the King had already landed.",
  ("Enemy-occupied territory—that is what this world is.",MC,"Jesus came into a world with real evil in it, to save it.")),
"2026-12-29":("Picture an old man who has waited his whole life at a train station for someone special. Finally the train pulls in, and he holds them in his arms. Now he can go home happy. That’s Simeon tonight.",None),
"2026-12-30":("Lewis said that when we really enjoy something, we can’t help telling people about it. Anna had waited for years, and when she saw the baby Jesus she couldn’t keep quiet.",None),
"2026-12-31":("The last lines of the Narnia books say the end of the story is really just the beginning: a story that goes on forever, where every chapter is better than the one before. Tonight we turn the page to a new year, held by the same faithful God.",
  ("…in which every chapter is better than the one before.",LB,"For God’s children, the best chapters are still ahead.")),
"2027-01-01":("In Narnia, being named by Aslan means everything. Lewis knew a name tells who you belong to. Tonight Jesus receives His name, the same name we start every devotion with, and the same name God put on you in Baptism.",None),
"2027-01-02":("In The Horse and His Boy, Shasta walks all night through fog on a strange road, scared and alone, until he realizes something huge is walking right beside him in the dark. It’s Aslan, and he’s been there the whole time. Tonight Jesus’ family has to move to a strange land.",None),
"2027-01-03":("Picture a kid lost at a giant store, and his parents finally find him in the one aisle he loves most. Lewis would say you can tell what someone loves by where they go when they’re free. Twelve-year-old Jesus is found in His Father’s house.",None),
"2027-01-04":("In Prince Caspian, Lucy sees Aslan again after a long time and says, “You’re bigger.” Aslan tells her He isn’t bigger, but every year she grows, she will find Him bigger. Tonight we hear that Jesus grew up too.",
  ("Every year you grow, you will find me bigger.",PC,"The more you grow, the more you’ll see how big Jesus really is.")),
"2027-01-05":("Imagine a man paid to shout a curse who opens his mouth and hears a blessing come out instead. Lewis loved how God turns the enemy’s plans upside down. Tonight even a talking donkey can’t stop God’s promise of a Star.",None),
"2027-01-06":("Lewis said every longing we have that nothing in this world can satisfy is a clue that we were made for something more. The wise men followed that longing across the desert, and found what they were made for: Jesus.",
  ("If I find in myself a desire which no experience in this world can satisfy, the most probable explanation is that I was made for another world.",MC,"The wise men’s search ended at Jesus. Ours does too.")),
"2027-01-07":("Picture one candle lighting another, then another, all the way down a long row, until the whole church glows. Somebody lit the first one. Tonight the light of Jesus starts spreading to the nations, all the way to our family.",None),
"2027-01-08":("In The Voyage of the Dawn Treader, greedy Eustace turns into a dragon. He tries to scratch off his dragon skin himself, again and again, but it always grows back. Finally Aslan tears it off, which hurts, and then washes him in a pool, and he comes out a boy again. Naaman washes in the Jordan tonight and comes out new.",
  ("The very first tear he made was so deep that I thought it had gone right into my heart.",VDT,"We can’t scrub off our own sin. God washes us clean in Baptism.")),
"2027-01-09":("Suppose you found a treasure map but couldn’t read the language. Then someone sits down beside you and says, “I can read that. It’s about you.” That’s what Philip does for the traveler tonight.",None),
"2027-01-10":("In The Silver Chair, Jill is terribly thirsty, but a lion is lying by the only stream. She asks if there’s another stream somewhere. The lion says there is no other stream. She has to come to him to drink. Tonight Jesus steps into the Jordan for us.",
  ("There is no other stream.",SC,"Jesus is the only way to life, and He comes to us in the water of Baptism.")),
"2027-01-11":("Whatever we trust most and love most is our god, and three young men tonight would rather face a furnace than trust anything but the true God.",
  ("Aim at Heaven and you will get earth ‘thrown in’: aim at earth and you will get neither.",MC,"Put God first, and everything else falls into its right place.")),
"2027-01-12":("Picture a kid who knows his dad’s phone number by heart. When he’s lost or scared, he doesn’t have to think. He just calls. God gave us His name so we can call on it like that. Tonight Peter starts to sink and cries out, “Lord, save me!”",None),
"2027-01-13":("In Prince Caspian, Lucy is the only one who sees Aslan at first, and she has to choose: follow Him, or go along with everyone else who’s busy and sure of their own plans. Tonight Mary chooses to sit at Jesus’ feet while Martha rushes around.",None),
"2027-01-14":("Lewis said love isn’t mainly a feeling; it’s choosing someone’s good, again and again. Ruth didn’t have to stay with Naomi. Tonight she chooses to.",None),
"2027-01-15":("Lewis gave simple advice for loving people: don’t waste time wondering whether you love your neighbor; act as if you did, and you’ll find you start to. Tonight a stranger stops for a hurt man everyone else walked past.",
  ("Do not waste time bothering whether you ‘love’ your neighbour; act as if you did.",MC,"Jesus is the best Good Samaritan, and He sends us to help too.")),
"2027-01-16":("In his book Miracles, Lewis pointed out that every year God turns water into wine slowly, through rain, vines, and grapes. At Cana, Jesus did the same thing all at once, showing He is the Creator. And He did it at a wedding, the good gift God gave in the garden.",None),
"2027-01-17":("When Edmund comes back from the White Witch, Aslan talks with him alone. Then He brings him to his brother and sisters and says there’s no need to talk to him about what is past. Edmund is simply forgiven. Tonight Jesus walks up to a cheater in a tree.",
  ("God will make us good because He loves us.",MC,"Jesus came to Zacchaeus first. Love changed his heart.")),
"2027-01-18":("Lewis said friendship begins the moment one person says to another, “What? You too? I thought I was the only one!” Jonathan and David had that kind of friendship, and tonight Jonathan stands up for his friend.",
  ("What! You too? I thought that no one but myself…","The Four Loves","A true friend stands up for you, and Jesus is the truest Friend of all.")),
"2027-01-19":("In The Voyage of the Dawn Treader, Eustace finds a dragon’s treasure and falls asleep on it, thinking greedy, dragonish thoughts. He wakes up as a dragon himself. Coveting starts small and inside, and tonight a king wants a garden that isn’t his.",None),
"2027-01-20":("Imagine two kids picking slices of cake. One grabs the biggest piece without thinking. Lewis would say the hungry, grabby heart is never full. Tonight Lot picks the best land, and it doesn’t go the way he thought.",
  None),
"2027-01-21":("Lewis said God doesn’t give us happiness apart from Himself, because there isn’t any. Every good thing, from your eyes to your dinner, comes from His hand. Tonight Jesus points at the birds and says: look how your Father feeds them.",None),
"2027-01-22":("Picture something so precious that someone gave everything they had to get it back. Lewis would say that’s the right way to measure what you’re worth: not by what you do, but by what was paid for you. Tonight we hear the price.",None),
"2027-01-23":("We can’t make ourselves believe, any more than we can make ourselves wake up. Someone has to call us. Tonight the Holy Spirit comes with wind and fire and calls thousands to faith.",None),
"2027-01-24":("Picture a child asking a father who already knows what he needs and still loves to hear him ask. Tonight the disciples ask Jesus to teach them, and He starts with two words: “Our Father.”",None),
"2027-01-25":("Lewis said courage isn’t just one good quality; it’s every good quality at the moment it’s tested. Daniel had prayed every day for years. Tonight praying could cost him his life, and he prays anyway.",
  ("Courage is not simply one of the virtues, but the form of every virtue at the testing point.","The Screwtape Letters","Daniel’s faithfulness was tested, and God was faithful to him.")),
"2027-01-26":("In Narnia, Aslan’s kingdom often grows from very small things: one girl stepping through a wardrobe, one boy saying yes. Tonight Jesus says God’s kingdom starts like a tiny seed.",None),
"2027-01-27":("Picture a kid who trusts his dad so much that he jumps off the edge of the pool into his arms, even though the water looks deep. Tonight, in a garden, Jesus faces the hardest thing ever, and He trusts His Father: “Not My will, but Yours, be done.” He did it for us.",None),
"2027-01-28":("Picture handing someone your lunch, and they turn it into enough for a whole stadium. Lewis would say that’s what happens whenever we give God the little we have. Tonight a boy shares his lunch with Jesus.",None),
"2027-01-29":("Imagine someone forgave you a debt of a billion dollars, and then you grabbed a friend by the collar over five bucks. Lewis would say that’s exactly how silly our grudges look next to what God forgave us. Tonight Peter asks how many times to forgive.",
  ("Every one says forgiveness is a lovely idea, until they have something to forgive.",MC,"Forgiving is hard. Jesus forgave us everything, and helps us forgive.")),
"2027-01-30":("In The Silver Chair, a witch fills a room with sweet green smoke and tells the children there is no sun, no Narnia, no Aslan. They almost believe her. Then Puddleglum stamps out her fire with his bare foot, the smoke clears, and he says out loud what he knows is true. Tonight Jesus fights temptation the same way: “It is written.”",
  ("No man knows how bad he is till he has tried very hard to be good.",MC,"We can’t beat temptation on our own. God’s Word is our weapon, and Jesus already won.")),
"2027-01-31":("At the end of the Narnia stories, everyone runs “further up and further in,” and every step is better than the one before. Lewis wanted us to know the best is always ahead for God’s people. Tonight two men sing in a prison at midnight, because they know it too.",
  ("Further up and further in!",LB,"God delivers His people, sometimes right away and always in the end. Amen!")),
}
